+
+<body>
+<div data-shell-header></div>
+<main id="main">
+<div class="wrap"><ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Portfolio</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Games</span></li></ol></div>
+  <header class="plate">
+    <div class="wrap plate__grid">
+      <div>
+        <p class="plate__kicker">Wing 05 · The anthology</p>
+        <h1>Games</h1>
+        <p class="plate__lede">Games are their own discipline here, not a subfolder of software. A game is a systems problem, an interaction problem, an art-direction problem and a psychology problem arriving at once, and the only way to judge one is against all four.</p>
+      </div>
+      <p class="stamp"><b>1</b> entry<br>Design document only<br>Nothing released yet</p>
+    </div>
+    <div class="wrap"><hr class="plate__rule" style="margin-top:32px"></div>
+  </header>
+
+
+  <section class="doc">
+    <div class="wrap">
+      <div class="empty-state">
+        <h2>This wing is built. It is not yet full.</h2>
+        <p>
+          There is one entry below, and it is a design document rather than a game — the systems
+          are specified and the alpha scope is defined, but nothing has been implemented.
+          Presenting it as a release would be exactly the kind of thing the rest of this site
+          is arranged to avoid.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          So the wing exists, the presentation system is finished, and the shelf says what is
+          actually on it. It is deliberately not linked from the main navigation until there is
+          something here worth navigating to.
+        </p>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="doc">
+    <div class="wrap">
+      <h2 class="sec-head"><span class="idx">01</span> Entries <span class="trail"></span></h2>
+      <div class="grid grid--2" id="gm"></div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="doc">
+    <div class="wrap">
+      <h2 class="sec-head"><span class="idx">02</span> What a game entry will carry <span class="trail"></span></h2>
+      <p class="sec-hint">
+        The schema below is the one every future release fills in. A field with nothing in it
+        renders as empty rather than being quietly dropped, so an incomplete entry looks
+        incomplete.
+      </p>
+      <dl class="placard">
+        <div><dt>Genre</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Engine</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd class="empty">Released · Playable · Prototype · Experimental</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>My role</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Design goal</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Core mechanic</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Playable demo</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Source</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Development notes</dt><dd class="empty">—</dd></div>
+      </dl>
+      <p class="sec-hint" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">
+        Subdivisions — Released, Playable, Prototype, Experimental Mechanics — are deliberately
+        not built. Four headings over one entry would be filing, not curation. They go in when
+        the volume justifies them.
+      </p>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+</main>
+<div data-shell-footer></div>
+
+<script src="/data/projects.js"></script>
+<script src="/assets/js/cards.js"></script>
+<script>
+CC.renderInto("#gm", CC.curated(CC.byCategory("games")));
+</script>
